LOK: typed selection copies and transactional R macro batches

ElyTable runs R outside LOK. This bridge reads only a bounded selection,
then validates a complete typed batch before applying it in one undo list
bound to the active view.
Formula cells are read-only. Each write follows Calc's own rule for typing
into that cell (ScDocument::IsBlockEditable); format changes refuse a
protected sheet; merged ranges are refused. A refusal mid-batch undoes the
batch and clears Redo. The caller also checks the worker revision.
Each refusal carries a code (.uno:ElyMacroRefusal hands over the last one),
so ElyTable can say why: too many cells, locked, protected, merged, too big.

